DERIVED FROM, and in one place included:
  gpudad/so101_pick_cube (https://huggingface.co/datasets/gpudad/so101_pick_cube),
  by gpudad, licensed under Apache-2.0. Every camera pose,
  focal length, light and material colour in these scenes was fitted by
  measuring against frames from that dataset.

  INCLUDED from it, both under that same Apache-2.0 licence:

    1. figures/original_3views.png. This is real imagery FROM that dataset:
       three frames of episode 188, frame 16, as seen by its front, overhead
       and wrist cameras, composited side by side. It is reproduced here so a
       reader can see what the reconstruction is being compared against.

    2. The six numbers in run.py's POSE_ARM constant, which are that dataset's
       recorded robot state at that same frame, converted to MuJoCo joint
       angles. They are what makes run.py reproduce
       figures/reconstruction_3views.png.

  NOT included: no episode files, no trajectories, no actions, and no other
  recorded data from that dataset. figures/reconstruction_3views.png is OUR
  render, not their imagery, and POSE_CUBE and POSE_BIN in run.py are this
  project's own fitted placements for this world.

